Id: upd005w
Severity: WARN
Category: packages
Check: check_updates
Fix: Set gpgcheck=1 for the repository, and in [main].
References: dnf.conf(5); yum.conf(5)
Controls: CIS 7.3, 7.4; NIST SI-2; ISO 8.8; CE Security update management

A package repository installs unsigned packages: gpgcheck is off for
it, or for [main] which it inherits. A compromised mirror can then
serve trojaned packages, and they install as root. Signatures are the
only thing standing between a mirror and root on the machine.
